## 2. Interface contract — the frozen schema

Normative. IMPLEMENT writes this file with the content below; deviations are defects.

### 2.1 Root

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://paeos.dev/sakg/schema/envelope.schema.json",
  "title": "SAKG Universal Node Envelope",
  "description": "SAEOS-1 §4.2. Every SAKG node carries this envelope; type-specific content lives in facets (ECS, checkmark-7). Frozen at SAKG-1/F-ENVELOPE.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "id", "type", "namespace", "facets", "label", "summary",
    "provenance", "evidence",
    "status", "confidence", "valid_from", "valid_until", "falsifier",
    "coordinates"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "id":          { "$ref": "#/$defs/node_id" },
    "type":        { "$ref": "#/$defs/node_type" },
    "namespace":   { "$ref": "#/$defs/project_ref" },
    "facets":      { "$ref": "#/$defs/facets" },
    "label":       { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 200 },
    "summary":     { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 280 },
    "provenance":  { "$ref": "#/$defs/provenance" },
    "evidence":    { "type": "array", "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/evidence_ref" },
                     "maxItems": 512 },
    "status":      { "$ref": "#/$defs/status" },
    "confidence":  { "$ref": "#/$defs/confidence" },
    "valid_from":  { "$ref": "#/$defs/timestamp" },
    "valid_until": { "oneOf": [ { "$ref": "#/$defs/timestamp" }, { "type": "null" } ] },
    "falsifier":   { "oneOf": [ { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 1024 },
                                { "type": "null" } ] },
    "coordinates": { "$ref": "#/$defs/coordinates" }
  },
  "allOf": [
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/inv_promotion_requires_evidence_binding" },
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/inv_refuted_requires_falsifier" },
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/inv_superseded_closes_window" },
    { "$ref": "#/$defs/inv_entity_carries_its_type_facet" }
  ],
  "unevaluatedProperties": false
}
```

Field-for-field against §4.2: `id, type, namespace, facets, label, summary, provenance{origin,
author_kind, ingested_at, source_hash}, evidence, status, confidence, valid_from, valid_until,
falsifier, coordinates` — **14 top-level fields, all present, all required.** Nothing added at
top level; the only structural changes are *inside* `confidence` (D-1) and *inside* `evidence`
items (D-2), both recorded in §7.

`valid_until` and `falsifier` are **required-but-nullable** rather than optional (D-4): in a frozen
envelope an explicit `null` asserts "open window" / "no falsifier stated", whereas absence is
ambiguous between that and an emitter that forgot. This also makes "every field" mechanically
checkable in the corpus (§5 test T09).

