## 3. Data flow

### 3.1 Where an envelope comes from and where it goes

```
PAEOS goal reaches L16 and seals
        │  (post-seal, one-way — nothing SAKG does can affect this goal, §6.1b r1)
        ▼
I-OUTBOX  runtime/emission/outbox.py ──▶ append-only outbox record
        │                                  validated by bundle.schema.json (F-BUNDLE)
        │                                  which $refs THIS envelope for each node
        ▼  pull, never push
I-INGEST  sakg/ingest.py
        │  1. read outbox record
        │  2. assign  id := sakg://<producing-namespace>/<type>/<ulid>
        │  3. set     status := "candidate"            (x5 — always, no exceptions)
        │  4. set     confidence := {value: <prior>, method: "ingest_prior",
        │                            inputs: [], computed_at: now}
        │  5. VALIDATE against envelope.schema.json  ◀── the gate this node freezes
        ▼
I-STORE   sakg/store.py — append-only; refs are the only mutation (K4)
        │
        ├─▶ promotion    candidate -> canonical   requires >=1 EvidenceRef  (INV-2)
        ├─▶ supersession new node + `supersedes` edge; old node's valid_until closes
        ├─▶ refutation   falsifier observed -> refuted; node RETAINED       (INV-3, FPL-2)
        └─▶ recompute    confidence := f(evidence, derived_from, supports)  (S3, Delta-6)
        ▼
F-PROJ    projection SUMMARY tier reads: summary (<=280), confidence.value,
          status filter (default [canonical]); tags trust: "untrusted" (§3.3.2)
```

**Element-by-element, every field is produced and consumed** (no gap):

| Field | Produced by | Consumed by |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | I-INGEST (ULID mint) | store keying, edge endpoints, `why` paths |
| `type` | I-EXTRACT (§4.3 mapping) | facet binding, §5.2 traversals |
| `namespace` | emission (§6.1b r4) | namespace isolation, cross-namespace disclosure (Ω5) |
| `facets` | I-EXTRACT | type-specific consumers; future facet schemas |
| `label` | I-EXTRACT | INDEX-tier projection |
| `summary` | I-EXTRACT | **SUMMARY-tier projection unit (Ω3)** — the ≤280 budget primitive |
| `provenance.origin` | I-OUTBOX | audit; `why` path; sample-bias analysis (A4) |
| `provenance.author_kind` | I-EXTRACT / I-INGEST | trust weighting by consumers |
| `provenance.ingested_at` | I-INGEST | `as_of` time-travel (Ω4) |
| `provenance.source_hash` | I-OUTBOX | content-addressed re-derivation; idempotent ingest |
| `evidence[]` | I-EXTRACT (CAS hashes only) | INV-2 promotion gate; re-verification (§3.3.3) |
| `status` | I-INGEST then I-STORE | §5.1 `status` filter (default `[canonical]`) |
| `confidence` | I-STORE / S3 recompute | §5.1 `min_confidence`; §7 confidence-collapse withholding |
| `valid_from` / `valid_until` | I-EXTRACT / I-STORE | `as_of` windowing; decay (Ω4) |
| `falsifier` | I-EXTRACT | refutation trigger (K6) |
| `coordinates` | I-EXTRACT | cross-project / cross-domain retrieval (✓9) |

### 3.2 What never flows

- **No artifact bytes.** `evidence[]` carries `uri + hash + kind + reverify` only; the schema
  forbids `content/payload/body/bytes/blob/text` by name (§2.3).
- **No authored confidence across the boundary.** F-BUNDLE inherits the obligation to *forbid*
  the `confidence` property outright in producer-emitted records (§8 hand-off O-2). SAKG computes
  it; PAEOS never supplies it.
- **No mutation back into PAEOS.** Enforced elsewhere (`! rg -q 'import sakg|from sakg' runtime/`
  in I-OUTBOX's accept), noted here so the arrow is not mistaken for bidirectional.

