## 7. Design decisions

| id | Decision | Rationale | Reversibility cost |
|---|---|---|---|
| **D-1** | `confidence` is a derivation record `{value, method, inputs, computed_at, generation?}`, not a bare float | §4.2's own invariant ("derived, never authored") is *unenforceable* on a scalar — the authored and derived documents are byte-identical — and F-ENVELOPE's acceptance demands an invalid fixture for it. Follows §3.3's "structural, not policy" doctrine. The scalar survives at `confidence.value`, so §5.1's `min_confidence` filter is unchanged. | **Deviation from §4.2 literal text.** Routed as a spec clarification (§10). Low cost while S1 is unbuilt; high after F-BUNDLE and I-STORE land. |
| **D-2** | `evidence_ref` forbids `content/payload/body/bytes/blob/text` *by name* as well as via `unevaluatedProperties` | §3.3.3 is a headline non-authority guarantee; a future relaxation of `unevaluatedProperties` must not silently revoke it. Redundancy is deliberate and is documented as such in the `$comment`. | Free — pure addition. |
| **D-3** | Each node must carry the facet named `sakg.<type>` | ECS: an Entity with no Component is an orphan. Freezes the facet naming grammar that F-BUNDLE and I-EXTRACT depend on F-ENVELOPE to inherit. Additional facets stay unconstrained, so §4.3's extension rule is intact. | Moderate — changing the facet naming grammar later touches I-EXTRACT and every fixture. |
| **D-4** | `valid_until` and `falsifier` are required-but-nullable, not optional | Explicit `null` asserts "open window" / "no falsifier"; absence conflates that with emitter error. Makes "every field" mechanically checkable (T09). | Low — relaxing required is backward-compatible; tightening is not. |
| **D-5** | Timestamps are `pattern`-asserted (RFC3339 UTC `Z` only), not `format`-asserted | `format` is annotation-only by default in draft 2020-12; relying on it would make the contract's meaning depend on validator configuration. A frozen contract must not. | Free. |
| **D-6** | `bundle.schema.json` references the envelope by **`$ref`**, not by copy | One definition, one freeze; a divergent copy in the bundle is exactly how the two would drift. | Free now; expensive after F-BUNDLE lands. |
| **D-7** | Supersession is an **edge** (§4.4 Temporal family), not a `prev`/`version` header pair as in K4 §2.2 | SAKG is Zone 2, not the kernel store. §4.4 requires every edge to be an object carrying `confidence`, `evidence`, `context`, `valid_from/until` — richer than a hash pointer, and necessary because supersession can be cross-namespace and evidence-bound. K4's *discipline* (append-only, no DELETE, content-addressing) is honoured; its *encoding* is not copied. | Low — the envelope has no supersession field to remove. |
| **D-8** | Fixtures obey a single-fault rule, enforced by a `repair` patch in the manifest (T11) | A conformance fixture that fails for two reasons silently weakens the suite: the intended clause may not be the one that fired. | Free. |
| **D-9** | Corpus sizes are 14 valid / 15 invalid against required minima of 12 / 8 | Headroom on both sides, so a later fixture retirement does not break the `accept` count and force an unrelated re-freeze. The invalid side is 15 rather than 14 because D-8's single-fault rule split the frequency-promotion case into I03 and I15. | Free. |

